---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

// No contact FORM, deliberately. A form needs somewhere to post to, and the
// options are a backend (which this site does not have) or a third-party
// embed that would load tracking scripts onto a page whose whole claim is that
// it loads none. An address and a public issue tracker are honest and work.

const structuredData = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'ContactPage',
    url: `${SITE.url}/contact`,
    mainEntity: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: SITE.name,
      email: SITE.email,
      url: SITE.url,
    },
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${SITE.url}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Contact', item: `${SITE.url}/contact` },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contact QuickOper"
  description="Get in touch about a figure that looks wrong, a correction, an embed request, or anything else. Email or the public issue tracker."
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <article class="text-ink-soft space-y-4">
    <h1 class="text-ink text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Contact</h1>

    <p class="text-lg">
      A real person reads these. Replies usually take a few days rather than a few
      minutes.
    </p>

    <div class="border-line bg-surface rounded-panel border p-5">
      <p class="text-ink-mute text-xs font-medium tracking-wide uppercase">Email</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-xl font-semibold">
        <a class="text-brand underline" href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      If a number looks wrong
    </h2>

    <p>
      This is the message we most want to receive. If a figure here disagrees with your
      lender, your statement or an official worked example, please tell us — it is the
      most useful thing anyone sends us, and we would rather hear it from you than not
      hear it at all.
    </p>

    <p>To let us reproduce it quickly, include whatever you can of:</p>

    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-ink">the link from your address bar</strong> — it carries the figures
        you entered, and never the names you gave them, so it is safe to send;
      </li>
      <li>the figure you expected, and where it came from;</li>
      <li>your browser and device, if the problem looks like a display issue.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Corrections are made openly. When we change a calculation, the change and its date
      are recorded on the affected page.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Bugs and code</h2>

    <p>
      The source is public. Technical issues are often best raised on{' '}
      <a class="text-brand underline" href={`${SITE.repo}/issues`} rel="noopener"
        >the issue tracker</a
      >, where the discussion is visible to everyone and the fix can be tracked.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      Embedding a calculator
    </h2>

    <p>
      If you write about personal finance and want to embed one of these tools on your own
      page, get in touch — we are happy to help and it costs nothing.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      What we cannot help with
    </h2>

    <p>
      We cannot advise on your personal financial situation, recommend a product or
      lender, or tell you what to do about a debt. Nobody here is qualified to, and
      answering anyway would be worse than declining. See <a
        class="text-brand underline"
        href="/about">about</a
      >{' '}
      for where that line sits and why.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      Why there is no form
    </h2>

    <p>
      A contact form has to post somewhere. That means either a server — which this site
      deliberately does not have — or a third-party embed that would load tracking scripts
      onto pages whose whole claim is that they load none. An email address is less
      fashionable and more honest.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
